                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "58503881",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198277984478",
                            "num_reviews": 607,
                            "playtime_forever": 28,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 22,
                            "last_played": 1619657446
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I only played for about 30 minutes, and sadly I have to refund and suggest to people interested in this game to wait it out for some quality of life patches, bug fixes and overall polish. \nThis is a very expensive game for the lack of polish - hit boxes on edges and slopes are sketchy, you're never climbing UP an edge, you're wading through the sprites on the slope drawn beneath it.\nIt looks about the quality of the game I'm making in pixel game maker mV, only I'm just a regualr person. This dev has made some really good games.\nI'm so confused as to what happened here.\nBoshy is fantstic, and Wings isn't my fave, but it was an admirable and challenging effort into pushing forward a more full game than I wnna be the boshy. \nBut this game is sloppy, with floaty controls, quesitonable hitboxes, combat that is neither diverse, nor filled wiht \" tons of moves \" you seem to plataeu as soon as you get your tail. Im told to tail slam, okay... but how do I tail slam? no control on screen, no info in the menu, no anything - I have no clue. \nGame feels unfinisihed. \nnot recommended for now. \n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1574990319,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1574990319,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 71,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7496953010559082,
                        "comment_count": 9,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Sorry that you had a bad launch experience :(\n\nThere's recently been made a post on the game page addressing these concerns, hopefully the game is in a better state for you now and you're able to form a new overall opinion on the game.\n\n\"tons of moves\" was a mistake to write, as that amount can vary from person to person how they perceive it. There are 3 attack buttons each with their own directional inputs and different magic spells to unlock with their own variations. Maybe \"several\" would've been a better word, I'm sorry if it left a false expectation that there would be hundreds of moves or something like that.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1575768583,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
